fix(test): interpolate the compose file without a stack having been run (#228)

The new object-scope tests read the credential wiring by asking docker compose
to interpolate the file. Interpolation needs INNSEGL_SPIRE_PARENT_ID, which
register.sh writes into deploy/compose/.env when a stack is brought up -- so the
tests passed on a machine that had run the stack and failed on every CI runner,
which by definition has not.

The harness now supplies a placeholder. These tests never start SPIRE and never
dial the parent; they read what each service would be handed. Only the
variable's presence matters, not its value.

Reproduced the CI condition locally by hiding deploy/compose/.env: the tests
fail without this and pass with it.

